    definition: "A countable noun names something you can count one by one, so it has a singular and a plural form (banana, bananas). An uncountable noun names something you cannot count as separate units, so it has only one form (rice, water, music). Many nouns are usually countable or usually uncountable, and you must learn which group each noun belongs to.",
